{title: Let My Prayer Rise Like Incense}
{subtitle: Psalms 141:2}
{key: Eb}
{tempo: 63}
{time: 2/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Eb] | ×15

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Lord, I call to you, here
Listen to my voice when I call to you here
[Ab]Hear me, O [Eb]Lord
[Ab]Hear me, O [Eb]Lord
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Let my prayers be for you like incense
The lifting of my hands like the evening sacrifice
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Set a guard, O Lord, over my mouth
[Ab]Keep watch at [Eb]the door of my lips
[Ab]Hear me, O [Eb]Lord
Hear me, O Lord
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Let my prayer rise before you like incense
The lifting of my hands like the evening sacrifice
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Lord, have mercy
Lord, have mercy
{end_of_verse}
